⚡️🌍 Worldwide public debt is approaching record levels last seen after World War II and could soon exceed 100% of global GDP, Managing Director of the International Monetary Fund (IMF) Kristalina Georgieva said.

Georgieva cited excessive budget deficits, record levels of public debt and high debt-servicing costs as key factors affecting the global economy.

